{#-
  IDIOM: "at this occasion, put these things in this state."

  The commonest shape in the corpus -- 6 pistons across both authors, all
  active (census 2026-08-13) -- and the one the compiler could not emit at all.

  This is written from HOME ASSISTANT'S side, not webCoRE's. HA already has a
  word for "every day at this time" (`trigger: time`) and for "relative to
  sunrise/sunset" (`trigger: sun` with an offset), so the piston's loop-free
  intent lands as two native triggers and nothing else. There is no variable,
  no template condition and no helper here because the intent does not contain
  any -- webCoRE's `happens_daily_at` is a way of SAYING it, not a mechanism to
  reproduce.

  HA-facing names live HERE, never in Python (COMPILER_SPEC "Jinja2
  everywhere"): the weekday words, the service call spelling, the condition
  keywords. Edit this file to follow HA if it renames any of them.

  Expects: automations = [ {id, alias, when:{kind,at|event,offset},
                            weekday:[0-6], months:[1-12],
                            actions:[{service, entities, data}]} ]
-#}
{% for a in automations %}
- id: "{{ a.id }}"
  alias: "{{ a.alias }}"
  mode: single
  triggers:
{%- if a.when.kind == 'sun' %}
    - trigger: sun
      event: {{ a.when.event }}
{%- if a.when.offset %}
      offset: "{{ a.when.offset }}"
{%- endif %}
{%- else %}
    - trigger: time
      at: "{{ a.when.at }}"
{%- endif %}
{%- if a.weekday or a.months %}
  conditions:
{%- if a.weekday %}
    - condition: time
      weekday:
{%- for d in a.weekday %}
        - {{ ['sun','mon','tue','wed','thu','fri','sat'][d] }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{%- if a.months %}
    - condition: template
      value_template: "{{ '{{' }} now().month in {{ a.months }} {{ '}}' }}"
{%- endif %}
{%- else %}
  conditions: []
{%- endif %}
  actions:
{%- for act in a.actions %}
    - action: {{ act.service }}
      target:
        entity_id:
{%- for e in act.entities %}
          - {{ e }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- if act.data %}
      data:
{%- for k, v in act.data.items() %}
        {{ k }}: {{ v }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{% endfor %}
